sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    box rgba(16, 185, 129, 0.1) Mode A: Fixture Path
    actor User as User / Animator
    participant Browser as Web Client (Vite / Three.js)
    participant Fixture as Static / Public Fixture
    end

    box rgba(99, 102, 241, 0.1) Mode B: Real Inference Path
    participant FastAPIService as Python Backend Service
    participant Adapter as Inference Adapter
    participant Model as MotionBricks Models (PyTorch)
    end

    Note over User,Fixture: Mode A: Instant Zero-Dependency Startup
    User->>Browser: Load Application (http://localhost:5173)
    Browser->>Fixture: GET /sample_motion.json
    Fixture-->>Browser: CanonicalHumanoidMotion/v1 Payload
    Browser->>Browser: Validate schema & bind to procedural mannequin
    Browser-->>User: Display walking humanoid & enable playback scrubber

    Note over User,Model: Mode B: Genuine Motion Generation
    User->>Browser: Select "Connect Backend" & Trigger Real Inference
    Browser->>FastAPIService: POST /api/inference/generate
    FastAPIService->>Adapter: Validate Checkpoints (.ckpt LFS status)

    alt Checkpoints Unpulled
        Adapter-->>FastAPIService: Error: Weights are LFS pointers
        FastAPIService-->>Browser: HTTP 503 (Detail & git lfs instructions)
        Browser-->>User: Display Toast: "Mode B unavailable: Pull weights"
    else Checkpoints Ready
        Adapter->>Model: Forward pass through Root, Pose & VQ-VAE
        Model-->>Adapter: Raw 414-dim motion feature tensor
        Adapter->>Adapter: Reconstruct & Retarget to CanonicalHumanoidMotion
        Adapter-->>FastAPIService: Validated Canonical JSON
        FastAPIService-->>Browser: Return Generated Motion
        Browser->>Browser: Stream / apply to VRM Avatar
        Browser-->>User: Real-time animated VRM Avatar
    end
